# surface: dnir
# ONE COLOUR LANGUAGE, second surface. A dnir opcode and a duon method call are
# the SAME edge, so they take the same role — `callable` — and the card
# `opcode` is what keeps the two surfaces apart. Registers are PLACES (§0b).
place %0: i64
const %1 = 7
add %2 = %0, %1
ret %2
edge view buffer
